That is what colocalized() is doing. Calculating mass features with similar distributions. There is a colocalized() method where you simply provide an m/z value as a reference to find other features with a similar distribution to that feature.

It isn't vectorized on the reference, so you can't use colocalized() to calculating all feature correlations at once. You would need to do it one-by-one.

If you just want all pairwise feature correlations, and the data is relatively small and fits in memory, you can just use the base R function cor(): cor(t(spectra(x))).

